WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
The underwriter reviews Marcus's application and the producer's report.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:10.300
A recent treatment answer may lead to an attending physician statement,

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.740
often called an A P S.

4
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.780
That statement comes from the treating medical professional and can clarify

5
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.900
history, diagnosis, treatment or follow-up.

6
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.400
It is different from the producer's observations and different from a

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.500
newly ordered examination. The insurer may use several sources together.

8
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.020
A producer should arrange the authorized process, not ask a client

9
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.000
to rewrite the doctor's record.

10
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.340
If information conflicts, obtain clarification through the proper source

11
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.180
instead of choosing whichever version produces a better price.

12
00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:53.074
An insurer may request an examination, laboratory information

13
00:00:53.774 --> 00:00:56.814
or other permitted evidence under its underwriting process.

14
00:00:57.894 --> 00:01:01.714
The requirements depend on the product, amount and applicant facts.

15
00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.674
No examination does not necessarily mean no underwriting.

16
00:01:07.574 --> 00:01:11.654
Accelerated processes can still evaluate authorized information.

17
00:01:12.494 --> 00:01:18.034
If an HIV test is required, follow the applicable informed-consent process

18
00:01:18.034 --> 00:01:19.754
and protect the result.

19
00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:25.174
An agent does not diagnose HIV from appearance, behavior or a

20
00:01:25.174 --> 00:01:29.934
laboratory number. Do not promise that a medical condition always produces

21
00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:34.854
a particular outcome. The insurer evaluates permitted evidence under its

22
00:01:34.854 --> 00:01:38.894
standards and the law, with the required authorizations and notices.

23
00:01:39.972 --> 00:01:44.672
An investigative consumer report can include information gathered through

24
00:01:44.672 --> 00:01:49.872
personal interviews about character, general reputation, personal

25
00:01:49.872 --> 00:01:52.252
characteristics or mode of living.

26
00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:55.552
It is distinct from a physician's statement.

27
00:01:56.432 --> 00:02:00.872
Consumer-report rules protect access, accuracy and privacy.

28
00:02:02.112 --> 00:02:05.732
The insurer must have a permissible purpose and follow the applicable

29
00:02:05.732 --> 00:02:07.532
notice and disclosure requirements.

30
00:02:08.172 --> 00:02:12.952
If report information contributes to a denial, higher rate or other

31
00:02:12.952 --> 00:02:18.952
adverse action, the required notice identifies the reporting agency, states

32
00:02:18.952 --> 00:02:22.672
that it did not make the decision, and explains dispute and

33
00:02:22.672 --> 00:02:27.812
free-report rights. Even a partial contribution can trigger the notice.

34
00:02:28.686 --> 00:02:33.226
M I B is a consumer-reporting source used by participating insurers.

35
00:02:34.406 --> 00:02:38.386
Its information can alert an underwriter to facts that need clarification,

36
00:02:39.086 --> 00:02:41.466
including a discrepancy with an application.

37
00:02:42.586 --> 00:02:45.246
It is not a complete medical chart and does not itself

38
00:02:45.246 --> 00:02:47.186
issue or deny the policy.

39
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:52.206
Obtain the required permission for medical report information and investigate

40
00:02:52.206 --> 00:02:55.466
the actual facts through authorized sources.

41
00:02:56.266 --> 00:03:01.466
Marcus can request his consumer file and dispute inaccurate information using

42
00:03:01.466 --> 00:03:05.926
the stated process. Do not assume every person has a file,

43
00:03:05.926 --> 00:03:09.946
or that an old report proves the same circumstances exist today.

44
00:03:10.766 --> 00:03:12.326
Accurate current evidence matters.

45
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.300
A preferred risk meets the insurer's more favorable criteria and may

46
00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.980
qualify for a lower rate.

47
00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:25.120
A standard risk fits the insurer's ordinary assumptions for that class.

48
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.420
A substandard risk is an accepted higher risk and may receive

49
00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.040
a rated premium or other permitted terms.

50
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.800
A declined application means the insurer does not accept that application

51
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.740
under its current requirements.

52
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:44.220
Substandard and declined are not the same result.

53
00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.220
Classification depends on the actual carrier and product.

54
00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:53.540
A producer should explain the offered terms accurately and avoid promising

55
00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.220
that another insurer must make the same decision.

56
00:03:57.066 --> 00:04:01.906
A higher premium is not automatically unfair discrimination when a lawful,

57
00:04:02.106 --> 00:04:04.186
supported risk difference explains it.

58
00:04:04.886 --> 00:04:09.146
But stereotypes and prohibited classifications are not underwriting evidence.

59
00:04:09.866 --> 00:04:13.966
Maryland protects applicants against specified unfair treatment and restricts

60
00:04:13.966 --> 00:04:15.906
use of domestic violence information.

61
00:04:16.886 --> 00:04:20.126
An insurer cannot use a person's status as an abuse victim

62
00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.926
to take an adverse action forbidden by the statute.

63
00:04:22.926 --> 00:04:27.186
The statute separately permits consideration of mental or physical medical

64
00:04:27.186 --> 00:04:28.966
conditions regardless of cause.

65
00:04:29.566 --> 00:04:32.586
It also does not require payment to someone who willfully caused

66
00:04:32.586 --> 00:04:36.806
the covered injury. Apply the actual facts and the legal rule.

67
00:04:37.246 --> 00:04:41.226
Fair underwriting combines relevant evidence, lawful standards and a clear

68
00:04:41.226 --> 00:04:42.526
explanation of the result.
